      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Glad to see this is being tracked, as this is effectively equivalent to a Canny   I opened yesterday.  Speaking from a security POV, I don't see any meaningful difference when it comes to security between dynamically constructing VRCUrls, and forcing them to be prebaked into the World Build, as I am very skeptical that they have someone who does nothing but vet the VRCUrls baked into worlds that have been recently uploaded, and there's always going to be someone smart enough to outsmart a script.\n\nBut a nice compromise would be allowing dynamic URLs which address the site white list which they maintain.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
