  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "String/Image downloader has been implemented and there is a growing demand for dynamically generating URLs with Udon. However, I can understand that you are concerned about sending requests to URLs indiscriminately from the viewpoint of privacy protection.\n\nTherefore, we request a function that can generate VRCUrl at runtime only for URLs that are listed in the trusted URL list.\n\nFor example, you can use it in U# code like this:\n\n```\n\nvar urlStr = \"https://youtube.com/\" + \"?v=PWLPw4RE9Ig\";\n\n　\n\nVRCUrl resultUrl;\n\n　\n\nvar success = VRCUrl.TryGenerateVRCUrl(urlStr, out resultUrl);\n\n　\n\nif(success)\n\n{\n\n  videoPlayer.LoadUrl(resultUrl);\n\n}\n\nelse\n\n{\n\n  // `resultUrl` is null\n\n  Debug.Log($\"Failed: the host of `{urlStr}` is not allowd to generate VRCUrl.\");\n\n}\n\n```\n\nIf this is implemented, for example, it will be possible to read YouTube search results as a list of video IDs with String Downloader, create video URLs with `TryGenerateVRCUrl`, and input them to the video player.",
